Wick Chapter 4.

00:00:38.070 --> 00:00:42.100
Ok so the movie ends with John taking down
the Marquis but in order to do that he has

00:00:42.100 --> 00:00:46.600
to goade him into taking part in the duel
itself. In his arrogance once he sees that

00:00:46.600 --> 00:00:51.480
John is seeminly beaten he decides to take
Caine's weapon and he goes to shoot Johh.

00:00:51.480 --> 00:00:55.440
Wick didn't actually fire during the last
shot of the duel and he uses this opportunity

00:00:55.440 --> 00:00:59.870
to kill the Marquis and free not only himself
but also Caine and his daughter.

00:00:59.870 --> 00:01:04.110
However he's mortally wounded and he ends
up dying on the steps of the church after

00:01:04.110 --> 00:01:05.840
uttering his wifes name Helen.

00:01:05.840 --> 00:01:10.450
Now many people were shocked to see this scene
playing out as Wick was seen as this invincible

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:19.270
and unstoppable terminator that was the very
personification of the boogeyman.

00:01:19.270 --> 00:01:20.270
-

00:01:20.270 --> 00:01:23.100
Because of this many people have speculated
over the last couple of days that Wick is

00:01:23.100 --> 00:01:26.570
actually still alive and there's been a lot
of wires getting crossed over whether he'll

00:01:26.570 --> 00:01:31.990
return or not. There was a fifth John Wick
film greenlit along with four and thus there's

00:01:31.990 --> 00:01:36.130
been talk that they just haven't announced
that so people go with the ending. Wick is

00:01:36.130 --> 00:01:41.210
also due to appear in the Ana De Armas spin-off
the Ballerina and you can see how rumours

00:01:41.210 --> 00:01:44.060
can spread.

00:01:44.060 --> 00:01:45.060
-

00:01:45.060 --> 00:01:48.500
No not like Baba Yaga. However, Chad Stahelski
has been doing a lot of press over the last

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:54.200
couple of days and he's discussed an alternate
ending they shot and cleared up a lot of things.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:58.500
So originally Chapter 5 was in the works and
they were going to shoot it back to back with

00:01:58.500 --> 00:02:03.430
Chapter 4. However he said that they realised
they'd rather do one movie they can put their

00:02:03.430 --> 00:02:08.560
all into instead of making two concurrently.
The Ballerina is also set between the events

00:02:08.560 --> 00:02:13.660
of chapter 3 and 4 so it doesnt really retcon
the ending either.

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:16.959
Now as for that ending, when the director
and Keanue went to the studio to pitch the

00:02:16.959 --> 00:02:21.950
idea they kicked off and said that they were
insane for killing off their big cash cow.

00:02:21.950 --> 00:02:26.560
In an interview with the Hollywood Reporter,
Chad said that the crew ended up having to

00:02:26.560 --> 00:02:30.680
shoot an alternate ending for the film that
left John alive.

00:02:30.680 --> 00:02:33.800
When discussing it he said that they initially
werte unsurue over whether to do a fourth

00:02:33.800 --> 00:02:38.739
movie and they came up with the Why which
would ultimately be Johns Death. They realised

00:02:38.739 --> 00:02:42.770
that they'd kinda fallen into a formula with
these movies where there were the same sorts

00:02:42.770 --> 00:02:47.490
of beats and Chad even said that if he was
a fan then he would've watched Chapter 3 thinking

00:02:47.490 --> 00:02:50.740
'how is he going to get out of this, just
give me an ending.'

00:02:50.740 --> 00:02:55.100
So Chapter 4 was pitched as something that
the franchise hadn't tackled before which

00:02:55.100 --> 00:02:58.129
was consequences and a conclusion.

00:02:58.129 --> 00:03:02.019
He said that they very much felt like this
film should be a goodbye to John but they

00:03:02.019 --> 00:03:06.040
wondered how to give a proper one. Thus they
came up with the idea that's laced throughout

00:03:06.040 --> 00:03:10.840
the movie which is that a good death only
comes after a good life. He said that sums

00:03:10.840 --> 00:03:14.980
up the movie and that the entire film is about
an action packed thrill ride in which John

00:03:14.980 --> 00:03:16.560
gets his redemption in the end.

00:03:16.560 --> 00:03:20.030
Now Chad then went into the test screenings
that they did and the times that they showed

00:03:20.030 --> 00:03:21.830
the alternate ending to audiences.

00:03:21.830 --> 00:03:27.560
According to the director the ending was almost
identical all the way up to the funeral scene.

00:03:27.560 --> 00:03:33.030
We even had that play out exactly the same
however Johns Dog would longingly look over

00:03:33.030 --> 00:03:38.159
and from here we'd get it confirmed that John
was still alive. This is why we had that shot

00:03:38.159 --> 00:03:42.409
in the movie and also Winston and The Bowery
King discussing whether he was in heaven or

00:03:42.409 --> 00:03:46.689
hell. Because they said neither that also
implied that he was still alive and out there

00:03:46.689 --> 00:03:50.270
somewhere which is something we pointed out
in our breakdown of the movie.

00:03:50.270 --> 00:03:56.189
However the fact that Chad is saying that
all these ideas were eventually cut down means

00:03:56.189 --> 00:04:02.640
that the intention was indeed to kill him.
So put away your tin foil hats, John is intended

00:04:02.640 --> 00:04:07.269
to be dead...but...with it being Hollywood
you never know how they're gonna work stuff

00:04:07.269 --> 00:04:14.220
in. I'm talking The Ballerina introducing
cloning technology or something.

00:04:14.220 --> 00:04:20.950
Now this ending didn't go down to well either
and apparently after the test screening they

00:04:20.950 --> 00:04:24.860
realised that it wasn't a good fit for how
they'd made their movie. Everything about

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:29.530
it is centred around death and in bringing
back John it somewhat cheapened the message.

00:04:29.530 --> 00:04:33.199
They talked about how this film was about
him realising that he'd ruined so many of

00:04:33.199 --> 00:04:39.139
his friends lives and had killed hundreds
and hundreds of people in order to avenge

00:04:39.139 --> 00:04:44.430
his dog. Thus they wanted to give some finality
and consequences to that so they had him saving

00:04:44.430 --> 00:04:48.169
a friend before his death which acted somewhat
as redemption.

00:04:48.169 --> 00:04:52.300
In the end the studio told them that they
could go with whatever ending they felt strongest

00:04:52.300 --> 00:04:57.430
about. This is what we got in the final cut
with John passing away and his death being

00:04:57.430 --> 00:04:58.430
final....for now.

00:04:58.430 --> 00:05:05.889
Anyway this film is of course filled with
death, most notably Charons. Played by Lance

00:05:05.889 --> 00:05:10.509
Reddick the actor sadly passed away whilst
the creative team were promoting the film

00:05:10.509 --> 00:05:15.800
and this has been a tragic conversation topic
centred around the film. Lance died just as

00:05:15.800 --> 00:05:19.481
the film was being sent out to the press for
screenings and Chad talked about what the

00:05:19.481 --> 00:05:24.240
creative team felt upon learning this. He
said that both he and Keanu were massive fans

00:05:24.240 --> 00:05:27.990
of the actor because of the Wire and that
he was one of the first people they cast after

00:05:27.990 --> 00:05:29.740
getting Keanu for the role.

00:05:29.740 --> 00:05:33.039
He said that when they initially pitched the
idea for the first film that it was difficult

00:05:33.039 --> 00:05:37.400
getting people to show interest because they
said it was about a man who's dog was killed

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:43.990
and he got revenge. It didn't really work
in pitch meetings and thus many people turned

00:05:43.990 --> 00:05:44.990
it down.

00:05:44.990 --> 00:05:46.090
However they said to Lance:

00:05:46.090 --> 00:05:50.500
“You’re going to be Charon the gatekeeper.&nbsp;John
Wick&nbsp;is going to be like Greek mythology.

00:05:50.500 --> 00:05:55.800
It’s a fantasy film like&nbsp;Lord of the Rings,
but in modern day.” and he instantly got

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:56.800
it.

00:05:56.800 --> 00:06:01.440
Now cut to Chapter 4 and he said that when
they pitched the idea to Lance about his reaction

00:06:01.440 --> 00:06:03.400
to his death, Chad told the Hollwyood Reporter.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:07.819
“Look, I can’t tell you I love it. I can’t
tell you I’m not upset, but I can tell you

00:06:07.819 --> 00:06:10.620
that I don’t know another way to make this
movie this good.”

00:06:10.620 --> 00:06:15.110
Chad later went on to talk about how his characters
death is the catalyst in the movie that really

00:06:15.110 --> 00:06:20.039
kicks things off and it's a major driving
force for Winston. The Marquis didn't want

00:06:20.039 --> 00:06:25.190
to make Winston one as it would give people
a reason to fight. However, in killing Charon

00:06:25.190 --> 00:06:27.439
he very much made one for Winston who aided
John throughout the film.

00:06:27.439 --> 00:06:30.760
Now when talking about it Chad said:

00:06:30.760 --> 00:06:34.940
Cut to last Friday, we had literally just
got off the plane in Toronto, but it seemed

00:06:34.940 --> 00:06:40.220
to be a very exciting and positive time. All
the screenings had been going really well,

00:06:40.220 --> 00:06:44.710
and we’d been so fortunate to have good
responses. So we’d been talking to Lance

00:06:44.710 --> 00:06:48.770
probably every other day, and we had just
seen him during the L.A. press, We left him

00:06:48.770 --> 00:06:53.229
with a high five, going, “Catch you later!”
And then when we got off the plane, Derek

00:06:53.229 --> 00:06:57.000
Kolstad, the original writer who’s very
close with Lance and his family, called me

00:06:57.000 --> 00:07:01.390
and said that Lance had passed. We hadn’t
even put the bags in the room yet, and I made

00:07:01.390 --> 00:07:06.610
one call to Keanu. He answered and I was like,
“Hey, man. I gotta come see you in your

00:07:06.610 --> 00:07:08.990
room.” And he was like, “Sure, come on
up.”

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:13.780
So he opened the door, and I was like, “Look,
I have some bad news. Lance just passed away.”

00:07:13.780 --> 00:07:18.581
And after the initial “what the f***?”
shock, everything went quiet. And then Keanu

00:07:18.581 --> 00:07:22.379
looked at me and we were like, “This is
for him.” We only had two or three hours

00:07:22.379 --> 00:07:26.410
before we had to go on stage in Toronto and
do the thing again, but that’s obviously

00:07:26.410 --> 00:07:29.840
nothing compared to what his family and his
close friends are going through. So, for the

00:07:29.840 --> 00:07:34.060
next hour and a half before our screening,
we just told Lance stories, and we realized

00:07:34.060 --> 00:07:38.099
how lucky we were to have worked with him.&nbsp;
It was one of the most fortunate times in

00:07:38.099 --> 00:07:39.099
my life.

00:07:39.099 --> 00:07:42.860
Now the movie had been sent out to cineams
already and they said that it's extremely

00:07:42.860 --> 00:07:47.850
difficult to recall the DCPs that get sent
out to cinemas. However even before Chad asked

00:07:47.850 --> 00:07:51.720
Lionsgate to add something to the end the
Studio had been hard at work and they had

00:07:51.720 --> 00:07:56.960
been making calls and getting it out there.
They said that not every single screening

00:07:56.960 --> 00:08:01.910
will have the dedication added onto the end
but I saw it on mine and I know that others

00:08:01.910 --> 00:08:02.970
did.

00:08:02.970 --> 00:08:07.409
Chad did say that by the time it hits streaming
and so on that the dedication will be in place

00:08:07.409 --> 00:08:11.479
and that they can make sure that Lance is
remembered for the great man that he is.

